(p-155) In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.

Surah Al-'Ankabut (The Spider)

His statement, exalted is He: ﴿Alif, Lam, Mim. Do people think that they will be left to say, "We believe," and they will not be tested?﴾ We have already presented the discussion on the disjointed letters (al-huruf al-muqatta'ah) in full at the beginning of Surah Hud. The interrogation in His words, ﴿Do people think﴾ [Al-'Ankabut: 2], is for denunciation (al-inkar).

The meaning is: people are not left without being tested (fitnah), that is, without being put to trial and examination, merely because they say, "We believe." Rather, when they say, "We believe," they are tested, that is, they are examined and tried with various kinds of trials, so that through that trial the truthful one in his saying "We believe" is distinguished from the one who is not truthful.

This meaning indicated by this noble verse has been made clear in other verses of the Book of Allah, such as:

• His statement, exalted is He: ﴿Or do you think that you will enter Paradise while there has not yet come to you the example of those who passed away before you? Adversity and hardship touched them, and they were shaken, until the Messenger and those who believed with him said, "When is the help of Allah?" Unquestionably, the help of Allah is near﴾ [Al-Baqarah: 214];

• and His statement: ﴿Or do you think that you will enter Paradise while Allah has not yet made evident those of you who have striven and made evident the patient﴾ [Al 'Imran: 142];

• and His statement, exalted is He: ﴿And We will surely test you until We make evident those of you who strive and the patient, and We will test your reports﴾ [Muhammad: 31];

• and His statement, exalted is He: ﴿Allah would not leave the believers in your present condition until He distinguishes the wicked from the good﴾, to the end of the verse [Al 'Imran: 179];

• and His statement, exalted is He: ﴿And that Allah may test what is in your breasts and purify what is in your hearts, and Allah is Knowing of the contents of the breasts﴾ [Al 'Imran: 154];

• and His statement, exalted is He: ﴿Or do you think that you will be left alone while Allah has not yet made evident those of you who strove and did not take other than Allah and His Messenger and the believers as intimate friends? And Allah is Acquainted with what you do﴾ [At-Tawbah: 16]; and other verses besides these. Allah, exalted is He, has alluded to this in His statement here:

• ﴿And We did test those before them, and Allah will surely make evident those who are truthful﴾, to the end of the verse [Al-'Ankabut: 3].

The established Sunnah has also made clear that this trial mentioned in this verse befalls the believers in proportion to the faith they have (p-156) possess; as in his statement (ﷺ): "The people most severely tested are the prophets, then the righteous, then the next best and the next best."
